! mcp_bootstrap_p213.strap -- MCP printed page 213: the head of THE
! INPUT PROGRAM -- its V-prefixed SYN block (field offsets, index-
! register names, small constants) and the first data words (V VSCR).
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.220, read at 400 dpi, doubtful glyphs
! at 900.  Header, READ: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP  CARD ID
! CA000001  DIST. OF 3/01  3/01  PAGE NUMBER 213" (printed "CARC IC
! CA0CCC01 ... DIST. OF 3/C1" -- see THE CARD ID).  The heading row's
! LOCATION field is BLANK -- line 1 is an asterisk banner
! (docs/transcription_workflow.md step 1).
!
! THE PAGE.  56 lines.
!   lines  1-3   banner "********** THE INPUT PROGRAM **********".
!   line   4     SLC,$ printed at 224105.00 * -- the counter arriving.
!   line   5     a blank comment card ("-" only).
!   lines  6-41  36 SYN cards, V F .. V PCP.  They print the SYN value
!                in LOCATION with the "+" sign suffix and +00000000 in
!                BINARY (address-valued), except V H and V UB, which
!                print 000000.00+ and their value in BINARY (+00000040,
!                +00000004): pure NUMBERS (cf. printed p.171 K QUANT,
!                p.185 K REP).  The data-description column prints NULL,
!                or BU,100,10 = (BU,64,8) on V M1 (explicit) and on the
!                twelve SYN,$n cards (inherited from the index register).
!   line  42     SLC,$ again at 224105.00; line 43 CNOP, (no location,
!                emits nothing -- counter already on a word).
!   lines 44-56  V VSCR: DD(BU,4),3,1 / DD(BU,3),0 / DD(BU,2),2,2 /
!                DD(BU,30),0 / EXT(0,18) over BE,V SCR / DD(BU,32),,,,,,
!                -- the last card's sixth field prints on p.214 line 1.
! JOIN.  p.212 ends with a 64-bit word at 224104.00 (finding aid), so
! the counter arrives at 224105.00 = the printed SLC,$; p.214 opens at
! 224110.40, which is where the sixth DD(BU,32) field falls.  Contiguous
! both ways.  An independent witness: printed p.121's landed deck SYNs
! VVSCR at (8)224105.00 (its "VF,VVSCR" rows), and this page defines it
! there.
!
! >>> THE CARD ID. <<<  The header prints "CA000001"; the right-hand
! serial column prints the first letter as a closed glyph with a
! straight left stem on every card, DA000001 .. DA000049, against the
! oval 0s beside it.  The same header line prints CARD and ID as "CARC"
! and "IC" -- D worn to C.  Recorded as DA, settled by the serial
! column's ink; not checkable by the assembler.
!
! >>> V ID, NOT V IC (lines 17, 18). <<<  At 900 dpi the glyph after I
! is squared with a faint, dotted right side, in BOTH the label (line 17)
! and the reference (line 18); the true C of V CWR on line 15 is round
! and open.  Read as D with its bow worn.  Label-only: no binary can
! settle it (VID is used only inside this page's own SYN chain).
!
! >>> Q, NOT G/C (lines 19-20, 34-37). <<<  V RQB (line 19, referenced
! "RQB" on line 20) and V Q1..V Q4 print the Q tail inside the bowl at
! 900 dpi; the right side of Q3/Q4 is worn.
!
! V VSCR vs V SCR.  The NAME column on line 44 prints "V VSCR" (=VVSCR);
! line 51's operand is "V SCR" (=VSCR), a DIFFERENT symbol: its
! EXT(0,18) prints 0451074, the 19-bit half-word address 0o224436 / 0,
! i.e. 224436.00, not VVSCR's 224105.00.  The volume OCR (docs/ocr line
! 11578) puts "V SCR LXV P,V PDG" at 224436.00, a page not yet landed.
!
! LINE 52, "DD(BU,32),,,,,,": six null fields, each 32 zero bits (a
! null field compiles as zero (C22-6531 printed p.7; C28-6129 PDF pp.8-9)).  Five print
! here (lines 52-56); the sixth prints at 224110.40 as p.214 line 1.
! This card deposits all six, so this deck checks the sixth too and
! p.214's deck starts after it.
!
! CARD SERIALS: DA000001-DA000049.  Line 45 shares DA000044 with line 44
! (one DD card, two fields), line 48 shares DA000046 with line 47, lines
! 50-51 share DA000048 (the EXT pair), lines 52-56 all print DA000049.
! The sequence-number column (-0037 ..) prints -0068 on line 28 (V T5)
! between -0064 and -0065, and skips -0042: the T5 card was moved.
! Lines 23 and 41 print "*" after the sequence number, line 24 a "+".
! Lines 1 and 3 print "*" after theirs; line 4 prints "*" after its
! LOCATION.  Recorded, not explained.

VSCR    SYN, (8)224436.0             ! line 51 EXT(0,18) of BE, half word only (printed 0451074)

        SLC, (8)224105.00
! line  1  -*************************************************************
! line  2  -********** THE INPUT PROGRAM **********
! line  3  -*************************************************************
        SLC,$                                                ! line  4 * printed 224105.00 *
! line  5  -
VF      SYN,.32                                              ! line  6
VH      SYN,32                                               ! line  7  a NUMBER: prints 000000.00+, BINARY +00000040
VXXRG   SYN,262143.VH                                        ! line  8
VM1     SYN(BU,64),262143.                                   ! line  9
VFCD    SYN,2.                                               ! line 10  -NO. OF REMAINING JOBS ON RT WHEN TS REQUESTED
VX      SYN,0                                                ! line 11
VX1     SYN,VX.VH                                            ! line 12
VX2S    SYN,VX1.VH                                           ! line 13
VX2R    SYN,VX2S.64                                          ! line 14
VCWR    SYN,VX2R+2.                                          ! line 15
VNX     SYN,VCWR.64                                          ! line 16
VID     SYN,VNX.VH                                           ! line 17  printed "V IC" (D's bow worn)
VSU     SYN,VID.VH                                           ! line 18  printed "V IC.V H"
VRQB    SYN,VSU.VH                                           ! line 19
VRCNT   SYN,VRQB.VH                                          ! line 20
VFCNT   SYN,VRCNT.VH                                         ! line 21
VSTR    SYN,VFCNT.VH                                         ! line 22
VTS     SYN,VSTR.VH                                          ! line 23
VFCNX   SYN,VTS.VH                                           ! line 24
VU      SYN,$3                                               ! line 25
VP      SYN,$1                                               ! line 26
VT1     SYN,$4                                               ! line 27
VT5     SYN,$9                                               ! line 28
VT2     SYN,$6                                               ! line 29
VT3     SYN,$7                                               ! line 30
VT4     SYN,$8                                               ! line 31
VS1     SYN,$10                                              ! line 32
VS2     SYN,$11                                              ! line 33
VQ1     SYN,$2                                               ! line 34
VQ2     SYN,$13                                              ! line 35
VQ3     SYN,$14                                              ! line 36
VQ4     SYN,$5                                               ! line 37
VUB     SYN,4                                                ! line 38  a NUMBER: prints 000000.00+, BINARY +00000004
VRA     SYN,1.32                                             ! line 39
VPAR    SYN,3.                                               ! line 40
VPOP    SYN,2.32                                             ! line 41 (prints V PCP: the open O; pp.222-224 reference V POP)
        SLC,$                                                ! line 42  printed 224105.00
        CNOP,                                                ! line 43
VVSCR   DD(BU,4),3,1                                         ! line 44 (and 45)
        DD(BU,3),0                                           ! line 46
        DD(BU,2),2,2                                         ! line 47 (and 48)
        DD(BU,30),0                                          ! line 49
        EXT(0,18)                                            ! line 50
        BE,VSCR                                              ! line 51
        DD(BU,32),,,,,,                                      ! line 52  six null fields (53-56; field 6 prints on p.214 line 1)

!SYM VF     000000.40
!SYM VH     000000.40
!SYM VXXRG  777777.40
!SYM VM1    777777.00
!SYM VFCD   000002.00
!SYM VX     000000.00
!SYM VX1    000000.40
!SYM VX2S   000001.00
!SYM VX2R   000002.00
!SYM VCWR   000004.00
!SYM VNX    000005.00
!SYM VID    000005.40
!SYM VSU    000006.00
!SYM VRQB   000006.40
!SYM VRCNT  000007.00
!SYM VFCNT  000007.40
!SYM VSTR   000010.00
!SYM VTS    000010.40
!SYM VFCNX  000011.00
!SYM VU     000023.00
!SYM VP     000021.00
!SYM VT1    000024.00
!SYM VT5    000031.00
!SYM VT2    000026.00
!SYM VT3    000027.00
!SYM VT4    000030.00
!SYM VS1    000032.00
!SYM VS2    000033.00
!SYM VQ1    000022.00
!SYM VQ2    000035.00
!SYM VQ3    000036.00
!SYM VQ4    000025.00
!SYM VUB    000000.04
!SYM VRA    000001.40
!SYM VPAR   000003.00
!SYM VPOP   000002.40
!SYM VVSCR  224105.00
! VH and VUB: the !SYM checks the VALUE, read from the BINARY column
! (+00000040 = 32, +00000004 = 4); their LOCATION prints 000000.00+
! (the p.185 K REP convention).
!CHECK 224105.00 | 03 | line 44 V VSCR DD(BU,4),3,1 | 4
!CHECK 224105.04 | 01 | line 45 second field (printed "C1": C/0) | 4
!CHECK 224105.10 | 0 | line 46 DD(BU,3),0 (printed "C") | 3
!CHECK 224105.13 | 2 | line 47 DD(BU,2),2,2 | 2
!CHECK 224105.15 | 2 | line 48 second field | 2
!CHECK 224105.17 | 0000000000 | line 49 DD(BU,30),0 | 30
!CHECK 224105.55 | 0451074 | line 51 BE,V SCR under line 50's EXT(0,18) -- 19 bits, V SCR's half-word address | 19
!CHECK 224106.00 | 00000000000 | line 52 DD(BU,32),,,,,, field 1 | 32
!CHECK 224106.40 | 00000000000 | line 53 field 2 | 32
!CHECK 224107.00 | 00000000000 | line 54 field 3 | 32
!CHECK 224107.40 | 00000000000 | line 55 field 4 | 32
!CHECK 224110.00 | 00000000000 | line 56 field 5 | 32
!CHECK 224110.40 | 00000000000 | field 6, printed on p.214 line 1 (that deck emits nothing for it) | 32
